# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The site.
#
# Only two variables, both public, both optional. Unset any of them and the
# site still builds and runs - it simply uses the content compiled into
# `src/data/` and records nothing. Nothing here is a secret: `VITE_` variables
# are inlined into the browser bundle, so a key that must stay private can
# never live in this file. See below for the ones that must not be VITE_.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The `offer` edge function. The one thing the site reads at runtime, so a
# campaign can be switched on or changed without waiting for a deploy. Unset,
# the popup renders the campaign written in src/data/offer.ts.
# https://<project>.functions.supabase.co/offer
VITE_OFFER_ENDPOINT=

# The `intake` edge function. Records a copy of each booking request and
# enquiry for the desk as the guest opens WhatsApp. Unset, nothing is recorded
# and the guest is unaffected - WhatsApp still opens with the same message.
# https://<project>.functions.supabase.co/intake
VITE_INTAKE_ENDPOINT=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build only - NOT prefixed VITE_, and that is deliberate.
#
# `scripts/sync-content.mjs` reads these to pull the content down once per
# build. The service_role key bypasses every access rule in the database; a
# `VITE_` prefix would compile it into the bundle and hand it to every visitor.
# Set these on the deploy platform as build environment variables, never here
# in a file that ships.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SUPABASE_URL=https://<project>.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
